<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI25-BLOCK-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI25-BLOCK-001" ;
  triage:title "ReleaseVersion::parse rejects the project's actual `beta-NN` prerelease format, requires `beta.NN` instead -- breaks CI and will panic ReleaseVersion::current() at the next beta version bump" ;
  triage:description """crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs ReleaseVersion::parse (around line 96) splits the version string on the first '-' into core/prerelease, then requires the prerelease segment to satisfy prerelease.starts_with("beta.") followed by all-ASCII-digit bytes. The project's actual prerelease format is `beta-NN` (hyphen-separated, e.g. `1.3.2-beta-24` as documented in README.md and referenced by AI24-MINOR-106), not `beta.NN` (dot-separated). Parsing `v1.3.2-beta-24` therefore splits into core=`1.3.2`, prerelease=`beta-24`, which fails the `starts_with("beta.")` check and returns AtmErrorCode::ClientDaemonVersionIncompatible instead of succeeding. This is a real parser defect, not just a stale test: ReleaseVersion::current() calls Self::parse(env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")).expect(...) -- if/when the crate version is bumped to a `-beta-NN` suffix (as the README already anticipates for 1.3.2), this will panic at daemon startup. Currently masked because Cargo.toml version is still 1.3.1 (no prerelease suffix), so no runtime panic yet -- but confirmed CI-red today via two failing tests: protocol::tests::release_version_accepts_semver_prereleases_and_rejects_non_semver (asserts `v1.3.2-beta-24` parses successfully; commit 6776b530dffad35ae44336f092be6d9ba0e2687b fails this) and protocol::tests::release_version_rejects_invalid_wire_deserialization (asserts the wire-deserialization error message contains "unexpected character"; current error message is "invalid ATM release version `{value}`", which does not contain that substring -- a second, independent assertion mismatch in the same function's error-message text). Confirmed identical failure on all 3 OS legs (ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest) of CI run 30197603631 on PR #640 (feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution @ 6776b530), so this is not a platform-specific issue -- it is a real logic defect. Hard merge-blocking: Test (ubuntu/macos/windows-latest) all fail on PR #640.""" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci-gate" ;
